\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Independent notebook V044-A-01.

Define \(g_{1}\) as the reviewed output symbol for this notebook.

The cobalt panel is the active scope; a separate ochre panel studies an unrelated response.

Within the cobalt panel, f subscript one is differentiable with respect to x subscript one.

The derivative entry is.

\[g_{1}=\frac{d f_{1}}{d x_{1}}\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Independent notebook V044-A-05.

Define \(z_{5}\) as the reviewed output symbol for this notebook.

The slate control note reuses A subscript five for both a shelf label and an undeclared mathematical token.

The star operator is never defined, and no derivative, input matrix, or compatible dimensions are supplied.

The isolated mark is.

\[z_{5}=A_{5}\star u_{5}\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Independent notebook V044-A-11.

Define \(d_{11}\) as the reviewed output symbol for this notebook.

The finite undirected graph G subscript eleven is the selected scope; a directed sketch H is explicitly separate.

Here d subscript eleven is the sum of all vertex degrees and e subscript eleven is the edge count of G.

Counting each endpoint yields.

\[d_{11}=2e_{11}\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Independent notebook V044-A-15.

Define \(\Psi_{15}\) as the reviewed output symbol for this notebook.

The triangle token is also a sample-bin marker, and no mathematical operation is assigned to it.

Neither a shear stress nor a shear rate is bound, so the nearby viscosity name cannot complete a Newtonian relation.

The isolated formula is.

\[\Psi_{15}=\mu_{15}\triangle v_{15}\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Independent notebook V044-A-17.

Define \(Q_{17}\) as the reviewed output symbol for this notebook.

The derivation multiplies section area by a reported speed.

The report identifies v subscript seventeen as centerline speed and never supplies an area-mean normal velocity.

Its provisional last line is.

\[Q_{17}=A_{17}v_{17}\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Independent notebook V044-A-21-INITIAL.

Define \(p_{21}\) as the reviewed output symbol for this notebook.

The initial sheet names two events but leaves the conditioning requirement unchecked.

Its incomplete draft is.

\[p_{21}=\Pr(A_{21}\cap B_{21})\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Independent notebook V044-A-21.

Define \(p_{21}\) as the reviewed output symbol for this notebook.

The revised sheet binds events A subscript twenty-one and B subscript twenty-one to one probability space.

It also states that the probability of B subscript twenty-one is positive.

The reviewed conditional entry is.

\[p_{21}=\frac{\Pr(A_{21}\cap B_{21})}{\Pr(B_{21})}\]
\end{document}

